{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:37:58Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 43, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tDesign written to `docs/design.md`. Summary of the key decisions the developer will implement against:\n2\t\n3\t- **New component** `frontend/src/components/SearchTasks.jsx` \u2014 a controlled `type=\"search\"` input (gets a native \u00d7 clear button for free in Chromium/Safari), `aria-label=\"Search tasks by title\"`, placeholder `\"Search by title\"`.\n4\t- **Layout**: wrap `SearchTasks` + `TaskFilter` in a new `.toolbar-filters` div inside `.list-toolbar`, search first, so `space-between` still spaces exactly two groups (filters | ClearCompleted) instead of drifting search away from the filter buttons.\n5\t- **Filtering**: two-pass filter in `App.jsx` \u2014 `stateFiltered` (today's logic, unchanged) then a search pass (trimmed, lower-cased, plain `.includes()`, never a regex). Pass `stateFiltered.length > 0` down to `TaskList` so it can tell \"state filter is empty\" apart from \"search found nothing.\"\n6\t- **Empty-state copy**: new `No tasks match \"{term}\".` string, added to `TaskList.jsx`'s empty-state logic with a defined precedence (empty store \u2192 existing per-filter copy; empty state-filter \u2192 existing copy; non-empty state-filter narrowed to zero by search \u2192 new copy). Also flagged adding `aria-live=\"polite\"` to the empty `<p>` since results now change live as the user types.\n7\t- **Styling**: reuses existing tokens only (`#ccd2d6` border, `#16191c` text, `#6b7780` placeholder/muted text) \u2014 computed contrast ratios (17.65:1 and 4.59:1) confirm no regressions, no new colors introduced.\n8\t- Full ASCII wireframes for every state (populated, narrowed, combined-with-filter, no-match, cleared, empty-store, loading, focus/native-clear) and a traceability table mapping every AC and edge case to a specific design element are in the doc.\n9\t\n10\tNext stage is `developer`, working from `docs/spec.md` + `docs/design.md`.", "meta": {"nati