{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:37:59Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 45, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tAll four files match the design plan. Implementation complete.\n2\t\n3\t## Handoff\n4\t\n5\t**Scope:** frontend only, for Taiga #11 (Search tasks by title). All changes match `docs/spec.md` + `docs/design.md`.\n6\t\n7\t**Files changed:**\n8\t- **`frontend/src/components/SearchTasks.jsx`** (new) \u2014 controlled `type=\"search\"` input, `value`/`onChange` props, `aria-label=\"Search tasks by title\"`, `placeholder=\"Search by title\"`. Matches `TaskFilter`'s prop shape.\n9\t- **`frontend/src/App.jsx`** \u2014 added `search` state (`App.jsx:16`, next to `filter`); split the single-pass filter into `stateFiltered` (unchanged open/done/all logic) then `visibleTasks` (search pass: `search.trim().toLowerCase()`, plain `.title.toLowerCase().includes(term)` \u2014 no regex, so literal `(`/`*`/etc. never throw, and an all-whitespace term trims to `''` which `.includes()` matches against everything); wrapped `SearchTasks` + `TaskFilter` in a new `.toolbar-filters` div inside `.list-toolbar` (search first, left of the state buttons) so `ClearCompleted` still gets the other half of `space-between`; passed `search` and `hasFilterResults={stateFiltered.length > 0}` down to `TaskList`.\n10\t- **`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`** \u2014 empty-state branch now picks between the new `No tasks match \"{term}\".` copy (when the state filter had results but search narrowed to zero) and the existing per-filter `EMPTY_COPY` (empty store, or state filter itself empty) \u2014 exactly the precedence table in the design doc. Added `aria-live=\"polite\"` to the `<p className=\"empty\">` uniformly across all four messages.\n11\t- **`frontend/src/App.css`** \u2014 added `.toolbar-filters` (flex row, wraps, `0.6rem` gap) and `.search-tasks input` (same border/radius/padding tokens as every other input in the app \u2014 no new colors).\n12\t\n13\t**Deviations from design:** none \u2014 implementation follows the doc's markup, prop shapes, filtering algorithm, and CSS verbatim.\n14\t\n15\t**Verification:**\n16\t- `npm run build` (Vite production build) passed cleanly \u2014 23 modules transformed, no errors. This exercises JSX parsing/compilation across all touched and new files.\n17\t- `npm run lint` (oxlint) \u2014 **could not run**: every invocation I tried (`npm run lint`, `npx oxlint src`, the `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint` binary directly) came back `This command requires approval`, in a headless session with no one able to grant it. This is a tooling/session limitation, not a code issue \u2014 I did not skip it by choice. Please run `cd frontend && npm run lint` before merging to confirm.\n18\t- No frontend test framework exists in this repo (`package.json` has no `test` script, no test deps, and no existing component has a test file), so there was nothing to add a test to or run \u2014 consistent with the rest of the codebase.\n19\t- Not manually exercised in a browser in this session (no browser tool available here); the design doc's wireframes cover every state (populated/narrowed/combined-with-filter/no-match/cleared/empty-store/loading/focus). Recommend a quick manual pass: `cd frontend && npm run dev`, type into the search box while toggling Open/Done/All, and confirm the \u201cNo tasks match\u2026\u201d message and native \u00d7 clear button (Chromium/Safari) both behave as designed.\n20\t\n21\t**How to verify:**\n22\t```\n23\tcd frontend && npm run build   # passed\n24\tcd frontend && npm run lint    # blocked in this session, please run manually\n25\tcd frontend && npm run dev     # manual UI check\n26\t```", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MMdBEzn8SnDPrzqTzBoBi3", "session_id": "056c1922-269a-4d1a-896f-122a636f69fb"}}
