{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:38:37Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 88, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "178:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T12:36:21Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 178, \"kind\": \"message\", \"text\": \"No frontend test files exist (confirmed, matches the earlier review's finding \\u2014 no test framework to skip). Now let me write the test-review report.\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"text\", \"session_id\": \"883da05c-e4de-4dcb-87b6-541369cb42f9\"}}\n179:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T12:36:22Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 179, \"kind\": \"tool_use\", \"text\": \"Bash\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"tool_use\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01SdhQsqrEm4C7qrvBoJBMBd\", \"input\": {\"command\": \"cd /home/dev/projects/test-project && git log --oneline -5 -- docs/test-review.md 2>/dev/null; ls docs/\"}, \"session_id\": \"883da05c-e4de-4dcb-87b6-541369cb42f9\"}}\n187:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T12:36:48Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 187, \"kind\": \"tool_use\", \"text\": \"Write\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"tool_use\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01JUSdmugQwtgRvuFTz7U1v1\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/test-review.md\", \"content\": \"# Test & review: Taiga #11 \\u2014 Search tasks by title\\n\\n**Scope:** `frontend/src/components/SearchTasks.jsx` (new), `frontend/src/App.jsx`,\\n`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`, `frontend/src/App.css`.\\n\\n## Commands actually run this session\\n\\n- `npm run build` (in `frontend/`) \\u2014 **passed**, no errors, 23 modules transformed.\\n- `python3 -m pytest -q` (in `backend/`) \\u2014 **35 passed**, 0 failed. Confirms the\\n  backend is untouched and unaffected, per the spec's non-goal.\\n- `find . -iname \\\"*.test.*\\\" -o -iname \\\"*.spec.*\\\"` (frontend, excluding\\n  `node_modules`) \\u2014 no matches. `frontend/package.json` has no `test` script.\\n  Confirmed: this repo has zero frontend test files/framework today, so no\\n  existing convention is being skipped by not adding automated frontend tests\\n  for this change \\u2014 that gap predates this feature.\\n\\n## What I could not run\\n\\nStarting the backend (`uvicorn`, any port/host combination) and outbound\\n`curl` requests were both denied by the session's approval gate, and this is\\na non-interactive run with no one to approve them. I tried three variations\\n(plain, explicit host bind, sandbox override) before stopping per protocol\\ninstead of retrying indefinitely. **Consequence: no live browser/E2E pass\\nagainst the running app.** Everything below is verified by hand-tracing the\\nactual source against each acceptance criterion and edge case, not by\\nclicking through the UI. This is the one explicit gap in this report.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria \\u2014 traced against source\\n\\nAll line refs are the current file contents I read this session.\\n\\n1. **Typing narrows by title** \\u2014 `App.jsx:38-40`: `visibleTasks =\\n   stateFiltered.filter(t => t.title.toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm))`.\\n   Holds.\\n2. **Case-insensitive** \\u2014 both sides lower-cased (`searchTerm` at\\n   `App.jsx:37`, `t.title.toLowerCase()` at `App.jsx:39`). Holds.\\n3. **Substring anywhere, not just prefix** \\u2014 plain `String.includes`, not\\n   `startsWith`. Holds.\\n4. **AND-combines with state filter** \\u2014 two-pass filter: `stateFiltered`\\n   (`App.jsx:31-35`, unchanged state-filter logic) computed first, then the\\n   search pass filters that result, not the raw `tasks` array. Holds.\\n5. **\\\"No matches\\\" message, distinct from per-filter empty copy** \\u2014\\n   `TaskList.jsx:16-21`: when `tasks.length === 0`, shows the new\\n   `` `No tasks match \\\"${trimmedSearch}\\\".` `` only if `hasFilterResults`\\n   (`stateFiltered.length > 0`, passed from `App.jsx:80`) **and**\\n   `trimmedSearch` is truthy; otherwise falls back to the existing\\n   `EMPTY_COPY[filter]`. Holds.\\n6. **Clearing search restores the state-filtered list** \\u2014 empty\\n   `searchTerm` means `''.includes()` is always true, so `visibleTasks`\\n   reduces back to exactly `stateFiltered`. Holds.\\n7. **Search term survives a refresh** \\u2014 `search` is `App`-level `useState`\\n   (`App.jsx:16`); `refresh()` (`App.jsx:18-27`) only touches `tasks`,\\n   `error`, `loading`. Same lifecycle as `filter`, which already survives\\n   refreshes today. Holds.\\n\\n## Edge cases \\u2014 traced against source\\n\\n- **Empty store:** `tasks = []` \\u21d2 `stateFiltered = []` \\u21d2 `hasFilterResults =\\n  false` \\u21d2 always falls to `EMPTY_COPY[filter]`, regardless of search text.\\n  Correct \\u2014 matches the spec's required precedence.\\n- **State filter already empty (e.g. `filter=done`, none done), any search\\n  text:** same as above, `hasFilterResults` is false before search is even\\n  applied \\u21d2 existing per-filter copy, not the new \\\"no matches\\\" copy.\\n  Correct.\\n- **Non-empty state-filter narrowed to zero by search:** `hasFilterResults`\\n  true, `tasks.length === 0` \\u21d2 new \\\"no matches\\\" copy. Correct.\\n- **Whitespace-only search (`\\\"   \\\"`):** `search.trim()` \\u2192 `''`;\\n  `''.includes()` is always true, so it behaves as no search (matches\\n  everything the state filter already allows) \\u2014 no throw, no bogus `No\\n  tasks match \\\"\\\".` message, because `TaskList.jsx:17-18` uses `trimmedSearch`\\n  (falsy for `''`) in the same truthy check. Verified this doesn't regress:\\n  if the state-filtered set is itself empty, whitespace search still falls\\n  to `EMPTY_COPY`, not a \\\"no matches\\\" bug. Correct.\\n- **Regex metacharacters (`(`, `*`, `.`) in the search term:** `.includes()`\\n  is a literal substring method, not a regex construction \\u2014 no throw, no\\n  metacharacter interpretation possible. Correct by construction.\\n- **Search term longer than any title / no title contains it:** zero\\n  matches, same code path as AC5. Correct.\\n- **Clearing search while a state filter is active:** returns to exactly\\n  `stateFiltered` (see AC6) \\u2014 not the full unfiltered list. Correct.\\n\\n## Display consistency\\n\\n`t.title` is filtered against exactly the string rendered in\\n`TaskList.jsx:99` (`<span className=\\\"task-title\\\">{task.title}</span>`) \\u2014\\nno separate trim/case transform applied only for display, so \\\"matches what\\nis actually displayed\\\" holds precisely.\\n\\n## CSS / layout\\n\\n`App.css` diff adds `.toolbar-filters` (flex, wraps `SearchTasks` +\\n`TaskFilter`) and `.search-tasks input` styling reusing existing tokens\\n(`#ccd2d6` border). Matches the design doc's stated reason (keep\\n`.list-toolbar`'s `space-between` spacing exactly two groups: filters |\\nClearCompleted). No new colors introduced.\\n\\n## Verdict rationale\\n\\nEvery acceptance criterion and every edge case in `docs/spec.md` traces\\ncleanly through the actual, current source. `npm run build` is green: no\\nfrontend test framework exists in this repo to run: the backend suite (out\\nof scope but re-run per protocol) is fully green at 35/35, confirming no\\nregression. The one gap \\u2014 no live browser exercise of the running app \\u2014 is\\ndue to this session's approval gate on network operations (backend server\\nstart, curl), not any defect found in the code; it's called out explicitly\\nabove rather than silently skipped.\\n\\nVERDICT: pass\\n\"}, \"session_id\": \"883da05c-e4de-4dcb-87b6-541369cb42f9\"}}\n189:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T12:36:48Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 189, \"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"text\": \"Claude requested permissions to write to /home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/test-review.md, but you haven't granted it yet.\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"user\", \"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01JUSdmugQwtgRvuFTz7U1v1\", \"session_id\": \"883da05c-e4de-4dcb-87b6-541369cb42f9\"}}\n196:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T12:37:04Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 196, \"k